1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,333
Here is the augmented matrix of our system.

2
00:00:03,333 --> 00:00:06,250
Our goal is reduced row echelon form,

3
00:00:06,250 --> 00:00:09,648
where the solution can simply be read off.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:11,450
Picture it first.

5
00:00:11,450 --> 00:00:14,366
Each equation is a plane in space.

6
00:00:14,366 --> 00:00:18,533
The solution is the single place where they all meet:

7
00:00:18,533 --> 00:00:21,033
the point (5, 3, −2).

8
00:00:21,033 --> 00:00:23,116
Row operations change the equations,

9
00:00:23,116 --> 00:00:25,248
but never that meeting point.

10
00:00:27,866 --> 00:00:28,283
Next,

11
00:00:28,283 --> 00:00:32,866
R₃ → R₃ − 2R₁,

12
00:00:32,866 --> 00:00:37,106
which puts a zero below the pivot in column 1.

13
00:00:38,066 --> 00:00:40,983
Next, R₂ → (1/2)R₂.

14
00:00:40,983 --> 00:00:45,194
Now the pivot in column 2 is a leading one.

15
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:46,550
Next,

16
00:00:46,550 --> 00:00:51,133
R₃ → R₃ − 3R₂,

17
00:00:51,133 --> 00:00:55,373
which puts a zero below the pivot in column 2.

18
00:00:56,333 --> 00:01:00,083
Next, R₃ → (−2/21)R₃.

19
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:04,250
Now the pivot in column 3 is a leading one.

20
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:06,333
That completes the forward phase:

21
00:01:06,333 --> 00:01:09,317
the matrix is in row echelon form.

22
00:01:10,266 --> 00:01:10,683
Next,

23
00:01:10,683 --> 00:01:14,433
R₁ → R₁ − R₃,

24
00:01:14,433 --> 00:01:19,074
which puts a zero above the leading one in column 3.

25
00:01:20,066 --> 00:01:20,483
Next,

26
00:01:20,483 --> 00:01:25,483
R₂ → R₂ − (5/2)R₃,

27
00:01:25,483 --> 00:01:30,122
which puts a zero above the leading one in column 3.

28
00:01:31,066 --> 00:01:31,483
Next,

29
00:01:31,483 --> 00:01:35,233
R₁ → R₁ − R₂,

30
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:39,874
which puts a zero above the leading one in column 2.

31
00:01:40,866 --> 00:01:43,366
This is reduced row echelon form,

32
00:01:43,366 --> 00:01:45,866
and the solution reads straight off:

33
00:01:45,866 --> 00:01:50,514
x = 5, y = 3, z = −2.

34
00:01:51,133 --> 00:01:53,425
Let's check by putting these

35
00:01:53,425 --> 00:01:55,716
values back into each original equation.

36
00:01:55,716 --> 00:01:59,533
Each of them holds, so the answer is right.

37
00:02:00,133 --> 00:02:00,966
To recap:

38
00:02:00,966 --> 00:02:02,633
get a leading one,

39
00:02:02,633 --> 00:02:04,716
clear the entries below it,

40
00:02:04,716 --> 00:02:06,800
move to the next column,

41
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,621
and finally clear the entries above each leading one.

42
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:12,866
Now it's your turn.

43
00:02:12,866 --> 00:02:15,783
Pause the video and solve this system.

44
00:02:15,783 --> 00:02:20,008
Your answer is checked in the write-up, so no peeking.

